@startuml 04_player_shoot
title Gameplay Example — the player shoots (key "J")

autonumber

actor Player
participant "input.Adapter" as InputAdapter
participant "event.Bus" as Bus
participant "Scene\n(WorldScene base)" as WorldScene
participant "metalslug.Scene\n(embeds WorldScene)" as MetalslugScene
participant "script.Engine\n(Python VM)" as VM
participant "player_controller.py" as PlayerScript
participant "object.Manager\n(the World)" as World

== Frame N: the key press is only latched ==

Player -> InputAdapter : holds "J" (bound to action "attack")
InputAdapter -> Bus : Emit(ScriptEmitted{Name: "AttackRequested"})
note right: config.yaml: input.attack = "J",\nscript_events.attack = "AttackRequested"
Bus -> WorldScene : ScriptEmitted handler
WorldScene -> VM : CallOnEvent("AttackRequested", nil)
VM -> PlayerScript : on_event("AttackRequested", payload)
PlayerScript -> PlayerScript : pending_shoot = True
note over PlayerScript
  on_event only **latches** the request. The actual shot
  is decided in update(dt), same frame or (more often) the next --
  see the script's own comment on why shooting isn't done here directly.
end note

== Frame N (later in the same tick) or N+1: the shot fires ==

WorldScene -> VM : CallScriptUpdate("player_controller.py", "update", playerGO, dt)
VM -> PlayerScript : update(dt)
PlayerScript -> PlayerScript : reads facing_x, pending_shoot
PlayerScript -> VM : engine.emit("SpawnProjectile", {"dir_x": facing_x, "dir_y": 0})
PlayerScript -> PlayerScript : pending_shoot = False
VM -> Bus : Emit(ScriptEmitted{Name: "SpawnProjectile", ...})

Bus -> MetalslugScene : ScriptEmitted handler
note right of MetalslugScene
  "SpawnProjectile" is a **metalslug-specific** convention --
  MetalslugScene.Setup subscribes to it on top of everything
  WorldScene already handles (e.g. "SpawnEntity"), because
  aiming/clearance math is this demo's own rule, not the
  engine's (see ADR-012's sibling doc, frame_engine_migration_plan.md).
end note
MetalslugScene -> World : Find("projectile_prototype")
World --> MetalslugScene : the prototype GameObject
MetalslugScene -> World : proto.Clone("projectile")
note right: Prototype pattern (object.GameObject.Clone) --\nnever hand-built field by field
MetalslugScene -> MetalslugScene : compute spawn offset from the\nplayer's own PhysicsBody half-extent\n+ Projectile.SpawnClearance
MetalslugScene -> MetalslugScene : set clone's Projectile.VelX/VelY\n= dir * Projectile.Speed
MetalslugScene -> World : world.Add(clone)

note over World
  From the next frame on, WorldScene.updateProjectiles(dt)
  moves the clone by VelX/VelY every tick, and
  MetalslugScene.updateHitDetection() checks it against every
  active Enemy's AABB until it hits one, leaves the level
  bounds (DespawnMargin), or is otherwise deactivated.
end note

@enduml
